# policy/ .gitignore — defense in depth. Nothing in this directory should
# ever be committed: it contains signing keys, consumed-nonce audit logs,
# policy-event streams, and distillation watermarks. All of these are
# per-host runtime state, not source.
#
# The root <MEMORY_ROOT>/.gitignore already enumerates each
# file pattern; this catch-all is the safety net for any future file added
# under policy/ that a maintainer forgets to add to the root ignore.
*
!.gitignore
